 Que : Reverse an given string
Input : "abcd"
Output: "dcba"
//Program
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		String s1="shruti";
		String s2="";
		if(s1.isEmpty()) {
			System.out.println("given string is empty");
		} else {
			for(int j=s1.length()-1; j>=0; j--)
			{
				s2=s2 + s1.charAt(j);
			}
			System.out.println(s2);
		}
	}
}

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aproach:
Check for string is empty or not(null check)
Use a loop to traverse the string from the end to the start.
concate each traversed character of string and store it into new string
after entire traverse of loop we will print the new reversed string
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Time Complexity:
Still O(n) because the loop runs n times.
However, s2 += s1.charAt(j) is inefficient because strings in Java are immutable. Each concatenation creates a new string, leading to O(n^2) time complexity in the worst case.

Space Complexity:
O(n) because a new string s2 is created to store the reversed string.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Optimized solution: 

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s1 = "shruti";
        StringBuilder s2 = new StringBuilder();
        for (int j = s1.length() - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
            s2.append(s1.charAt(j)); // Efficiently append characters
        }
        System.out.println(s2.toString()); // Print the reversed string
    }
}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Time Complexity:
O(n) because StringBuilder appends characters in constant time.

Space Complexity:
O(n) because StringBuilder stores the reversed string
